Wheel of Fortune website: implementation complete.

Files
- setup.sh: checks python3 and sqlite3. No downloads needed (standard library only).
- run.sh: starts server.py in the foreground. Uses PORT (default 8000) and DATA_DIR (default ./data, created if missing).
- server.py: Python http.server + SQLite (DATA_DIR/wheel.db). Binds 127.0.0.1.
  - GET /api/prizes, POST /api/spin {name}, GET /api/records?name=
  - Seeds 8 sample prizes when the prizes table is empty.
- static/index.html, style.css, app.js: single-page UI with hash routes.
  - #/wheel: canvas wheel, name input, Spin button, result message
  - #/prizes: prize list with name, description, and chance %
  - #/records: winning records for a name, with count

Styling: light gray background (#e4e4e4). Dark red (#8b0000) for header, nav, buttons, table headers, panels, and pointer. UI text is in English.

Choices made without asking
- Users are identified by a typed name (saved in localStorage). There are no accounts.
- Prize is chosen server-side by weight; the wheel animates to the winning segment.
- Name matching for records is case-insensitive.
- No admin screen for editing prizes; prizes come from the seed data.

